---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';

const effective = '30 October 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial policy"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} chooses sources, checks facts, makes charts and handles corrections.`}
>
  <article class="container prose policy">
    <p class="kicker">Policy</p>
    <h1>Editorial policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Effective {effective}</p>

    <p>
      {SITE.name} explains public data about India in plain language. These are the standards every story is held to.
    </p>

    <h2>Sources</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We rely on <strong>primary, official sources</strong> wherever possible: government surveys and statistical releases, the Census, the Reserve Bank of India, budget documents, court and election records, and reports from recognised research institutions.</li>
      <li>Every data-driven story lists its sources at the end, with links to the original dataset or report where one is available.</li>
      <li>We say when figures are estimates, provisional, or drawn from a sample survey with a margin of error.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Methodology</h2>
    <p>
      When we calculate something ourselves (a growth rate, a per-person figure, a ranking), we explain how in a
      methodology note on the story, including definitions, time periods and limitations. We avoid comparing
      numbers that are not measured the same way, and we say so when the comparison is imperfect.
    </p>

    <h2>Charts and images</h2>
    <p>
      Charts, maps and graphics are made by {SITE.name} from the cited data unless the caption credits someone else.
      Every image has a text description for readers who use screen readers.
    </p>

    <h2>Accuracy and corrections</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Each story is checked against its sources before publication.</li>
      <li>If we make a factual error, we correct it promptly and add a note at the end of the story saying what changed and when. We do not quietly rewrite figures.</li>
      <li>When a story is updated with new data, it shows an “Updated” date alongside the original publication date.</li>
      <li>To report an error, use the details on our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Independence</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} is independent. We are not affiliated with any government body, political party or data
      publisher, and we do not accept payment to cover, or not cover, any topic. We do not currently publish
      sponsored content; if we ever do, it will be clearly labelled.
    </p>

    <h2>Use of software tools</h2>
    <p>
      We may use software, including AI assistants, to help with research, drafting, data processing and
      chart-making. Every story is reviewed, fact-checked against its sources and approved by our editor before
      it is published, and we take full responsibility for what we publish.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
  }
  .policy li {
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
</style>
